<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48772" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">transĕro</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trans-sĕro</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, sertum,
			3, v. a. * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To pass</i> or <i>thrust through</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per aliquid ramulum transerere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 133, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To transfer by grafting</i>, <i>to
				ingraft</i>: vidi ego transertos alieno  in
			robore ramos Altius ire suis, <i><span class="en">Stat. S.
				2, 1, 101</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
